From 10b8b4ca673c8f243b041e4dbffb3d8622e698ec Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yaegerbomb42 <yaeger.james42@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 21:52:35 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] fix(library): scope tools and permissions per role, harden
 staged imports

- a role only gets the custom tools assigned to it (the manifest and the
  seeded scripts are filtered, and the tools MCP server is wired only when
  the role has assigned tools)
- user-installed MCP servers and the library tools server are granted in the
  run's --allowedTools, so the agent can actually call the servers the user
  assigned
- a partial role-assignment update no longer wipes the other kinds (toggling
  a skill kept clearing the role's servers and tools)
- staged import ids must be slugs, so an id like ../../library cannot read or
  delete a file outside the account's staging folder
- e2e: dismiss the real first-run onboarding (Skip / Launch) before opening
  the Library

Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>
